what is food  food is any nutritious substance that  people or animals eat or drink or that  plants absorb in order to maintain life  and growth  my name is ben brown and i'm a filmmaker  working with great big story  i've always taken an interest in  nutrition but over the last few years  i've been asking myself  what does food really mean to me  every day we are confronted with endless  conflicting information about what we  should and should not be eating  sugar-free low-fat gmo msg naturally  added flavors as convenience and price  take priority over quality and health we  find ourselves becoming disconnected  from the food that sustains us  in search of some simple answers i  traveled to costa rica to meet a farmer  who abandoned the fast-paced city life  to reconnect with food by growing it  himself i'm henry henry karczynski i'm  manager of villa vanilla  a organic biodynamic spice farm i grow  spices here in the central pacific of  costa rica i started in chicago i grew  up in chicago i had a couple jobs i  remember getting in my car you know i  had  visit clients on the north side of  chicago i would like go right to the  drive-in  get my big mac and french fries and a  soft drink and then head out on the road  to my next contact i mean i would do  that  when i was 24 it's a rat race and  everybody's trying to struggle to get up  the ladder and then when they get to the  top they go what did i do with my life  you know it's already too late  and i had a sort of restart look at what  am i going to do and  a little seed started growing in me to  actually do my own thing i just had  something growing in me  to grow to grow plants to grow food  to do a farm and i was introduced to  biodynamics from the book the secrets of  the soil  i think the most impact that had was  that it removed those blindfolds and i  was able to see the  big picture  you know in a way a mission i have is to  use the farm as a  sort of a message for people to look at  at food  we are living on this planet and  we're also here to enjoy the pleasures  the food  the sensuality of living on this planet  food is a flavor it's an aroma it's uh  it's something to enjoy  so what i would actually recommend to  people that are starting that first  journey is start a garden grow your  tomatoes grow your lettuce you know make  that first step uh you'll be blown away  on how much  that how good that food tastes and uh  and you can be starting connecting with  mother earth  the most important thing is to get that  take that first step as i said at one  time i was a little bit  discouraged because of the environments  but recently there's optimism  there's lights  at that end of that tunnel  i share henry's optimism for change we  already know about the endless health  benefits of eating natural organic  produce  but i also believe that by improving our  relationship with food we can reconnect  with this beautiful planet  to consume consciously is to take action  against the destructive objectives of  large-scale food production  mother earth is a beautiful biological  system  so we must keep it simple  take responsibility  and work to protect the only home we  have  you

